@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps_landscape.pattern.delivery_scheduling a ds:Pattern;
    ds:name "Delivery Scheduling";
    ds:summary "Delivery Scheduling is a reusable Landscape form pattern composed from two independent Formik-bound blocks. Delivery Block chooses immediate delivery or reveals a local `datetime-local` value for scheduled delivery; Randomization Block chooses whether to reveal a numeric delay window that spreads delivery over a number of minutes.\n\nThe blocks can be used together or separately. Their components own labels, choice values, reveal/reset effects, and basic input attributes, while the exported Yup fragments own the required, future-date, integer, range, and optional expiration-relative validation used by consuming forms.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "node:\n  uri: ds:apps_landscape.pattern.delivery_scheduling\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        uri: ds:apps_landscape.component.expandable_radio_group\n        role: delivery time\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              uri: global.component.radio\n              role: as soon as possible option\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n          - node:\n              uri: global.component.radio\n              role: scheduled option\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.input\n                    role: deliver after\n                    attributes:\n                      type: datetime-local\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      slotName: expansion\n                      condition: scheduled option is selected\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"\n    - node:\n        uri: ds:apps_landscape.component.expandable_radio_group\n        role: randomization\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              uri: global.component.radio\n              role: yes option\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.input\n                    role: delivery delay window\n                    attributes:\n                      type: number\n                      inputMode: numeric\n                      min: 0\n                      unit: minutes\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      slotName: expansion\n                      condition: yes option is selected\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n          - node:\n              uri: global.component.radio\n              role: no option\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"";
    ds:anatomyClassic "https://www.figma.com/design/I4WpvwMuQI6v1qhgUl63Sx/Landscape-Pragma-components?node-id=17-22&t=iG2ObZ6Q1XG2A2MB-4\n\nTable 19\n\n";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n**Immediate or deferred work**\n\nUse when an operation can start as soon as possible or after a user-selected date and time.\n\n**Load distribution**\n\nUse when large fleets should receive work over a randomized minute window to reduce simultaneous load.\n\n**Composable scheduling controls**\n\nUse only Delivery Block when an action needs immediate/scheduled timing without randomization, or only Randomization Block when its base execution time is defined elsewhere. Source consumers use both combinations.\n\n### When not to use\n\n**Recurring execution**\n\nJobs that must repeat or follow a recurring schedule.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using Delivery Block/Randomization Block for cron-like scheduled operations.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use Recurring Schedule or Cron Schedule instead.\n\n**Fixed delivery semantics**\n\nAn operation where the timing is determined by policy and users have no choice.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Rendering choice radios when the system always delivers immediately or always on a schedule.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Omit the choice controls and render only the applicable delivery state or display as read-only metadata.\n\n**Date range or time-zone selection**\n\nRequirements to specify a start/end range, time zone, or calendar recurrence rules.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using the local `datetime-local` input when users must select a time zone or define a date range.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a dedicated date-range picker or time-zone-aware scheduling component instead.\n\n**Unvalidated standalone composition**\n\nAssuming that the rendered controls enforce all scheduling rules without parent validation.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Rendering the blocks without integrating the exported Yup validation fragments into the parent form schema.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Compose both `deliveryValidationSchema` and `randomizationValidationSchema` (or equivalent validation) into the parent Formik schema.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n- The current Expandable Radio Group renders each heading as a styled paragraph and does not wrap its radios in `fieldset`, `legend`, or a named `radiogroup`. This is an upstream accessibility gap, not a guarantee of the Landscape implementation.\n- Conditional inputs are mounted immediately after and indented beneath their owning option, preserving reading order, but selection does not move focus into them.\n- Labels for “Deliver after” and “Delivery delay window” are visually hidden, not absent. Preserve them and keep Formik errors attached through Canonical Input.\n- Reveal/hide is controlled by radio selection; do not require pointer hover to discover either field.\n\n### Content\n\n- State the time zone used by the delivery date and whether the randomized window begins at that time.\n- Use minutes consistently for the delay window and explain the operational reason for randomization when needed.\n- The source’s visible copy is fixed English. Localize group labels, option labels, hidden input labels, help, and validation messages before using the pattern in a translated surface.\n\n### Internationalization and time\n\n- `datetime-local` intentionally carries no time-zone offset. The five-minute initializer converts the current Moment value to ISO and slices it to minutes; consumers must verify that this represents the intended local/server semantics.\n- Do not translate Formik field keys or submitted numeric units. Translate only visible labels, help, and errors.\n- Allow longer translated group labels to wrap above the options.\n\n### Keyboard navigation\n\n- Radio and input keyboard behavior is delegated to Canonical controls; the pattern adds no custom key handlers.\n- A selected expansion follows its radio in normal Tab order. Selecting a radio awaits its state update/effect but does not focus the newly mounted field.\n\n### Device and layout\n\n- Expansions are rendered through the shared Indent layout beneath the selected option. Verify its indentation at narrow widths; these source files define no responsive override.\n- Native `datetime-local` presentation varies by browser and device. Do not claim a calendar picker or equivalent UI on every platform.";
    ds:tier ds:apps_landscape;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.specialadoption-docs;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "DeliveryBlock.formik ";
        ds:summary "Supplies values, getFieldProps, setFieldValue, errors, and touched state. ";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: Formik context with values containing deliver_immediately: boolean and deliver_after: string. Coda's property type taxonomy has no structured-object or Formik-context type. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "RandomizationBlock.formik ";
        ds:summary "Supplies the same Formik services for randomization. ";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: Formik context with values containing randomize_delivery: boolean and deliver_delay_window: number. Coda's property type taxonomy has no structured-object or Formik-context type. "
    ].
